---
title: Installation
description: Installing the stable Ergosfare v1 packages, and what you would install for v2 instead.
---

The stable v1.x packages are published to nuget.org and install without any flags:

```bash
dotnet add package Stella.Ergosfare
```

`Stella.Ergosfare` is an umbrella package pulling in the Commands, Queries and Events
modules with their DI extensions.

{% aside type="tip" %}
For a new project, consider the v2 preview instead — it adds compile-time registration,
Native AOT support and a `ValueTask`-first surface:

```bash
dotnet add package Stella.Ergosfare --prerelease
dotnet add package Stella.Ergosfare.SourceGenerator --prerelease
```

See the [v2 installation guide](/ergosfare.docs/preview/getting-started/installation).
{% /aside %}

## Picking packages

Each module is independent; the umbrella package is a convenience:

| Package | What it gives you |
|---|---|
| `Stella.Ergosfare` | Umbrella — Commands + Queries + Events + DI extensions |
| `Stella.Ergosfare.Core.Abstractions` | `IExecutionContext`, handler and interceptor contracts |
| `Stella.Ergosfare.Commands.Abstractions` | `ICommand`, `ICommandHandler`, command interceptors |
| `Stella.Ergosfare.Queries.Abstractions` | `IQuery`, `IStreamQuery`, query handlers and interceptors |
| `Stella.Ergosfare.Events.Abstractions` | `IEvent`, `IEventHandler`, event interceptors |
| `Stella.Ergosfare.Core` | Runtime: registry, pipeline, dispatch |
| `Stella.Ergosfare.*.Extensions.MicrosoftDependencyInjection` | `AddErgosfare`, module builders |

A library that only declares messages and handlers needs just the relevant `.Abstractions`
package:

```bash
dotnet add package Stella.Ergosfare.Commands.Abstractions
```

On v1 that library's handlers still have to be registered by the application, which means
the application must scan the library's assembly explicitly:

```csharp
.AddCommandModule(c => c
    .RegisterFromAssembly(Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly())
    .RegisterFromAssembly(typeof(SomeTypeInTheLibrary).Assembly))
```

On v2 the source generator walks referenced assemblies for you and the second call
disappears — see
[Compile-time discovery](/ergosfare.docs/preview/core-concepts/compile-time-discovery).

## Requirements

The v1 line targets `net9.0` and `net10.0`.

## Versioning

| Branch | Line | Tags | NuGet |
|---|---|---|---|
| `main` | stable v1.x | `vX.Y.Z` | stable |
| `preview` | v2 | `v2.0.0-preview.N` | pre-release |

Stable fixes land on `main` first and are merged into `preview` regularly, so nothing you
depend on here disappears when you move up. The full policy is in
[COMPATIBILITY.md](https://github.com/stellayazilim/ergosfare/blob/main/COMPATIBILITY.md).

